iversity of Glasgow</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gakidou</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Murray</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Frenk</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Defining and measuring health inequality</article-title><source>Bulletin of the World Health Organisation</source><year>2000</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>42</fpage><lpage>52</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Doorslaer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inequalities in self-reported health: validation of a new approach to measurement</article-title><source>Journal of Health Economics</source><year>2003</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>61</fpage><lpage>87</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12564718</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0167-6296(02)00080-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kakwani</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name><name><surname>Wagstaff</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>van Doorslaer</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Socio-economic inequalities in health: measurement, computation and statistical inference</article-title><source>Journal of Econometrics</source><year>1997</year><volume>77</volume><fpage>87</fpage><lpage>103</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0304-4076(96)01807-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DeWilde</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Carey</surname><given-names>IM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bremner</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Richards</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilton</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of Statin prescribing 1994&#x02013;2001: a case of ageism but not of sexism</article-title><source>Heart</source><year>2003</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>417</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12639870</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/heart.89.4.417</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>